2. Consolidated Group & Affiliate Scope ("You")
For all thresholds below, "You" includes the receiving legal entity and all
of its direct or indirect Affiliates (any entity controlling, controlled by, or
under common control with You, whether through majority equity ownership,
voting power, board authority, or de facto management control). Revenue and
monthly active user (MAU) metrics are calculated on an aggregate,
consolidated group basis across You and all Affiliates over the trailing
twelve (12) consecutive months.

3. UI Attribution Requirement (Products > 1M MAU or > $1M Annual Revenue)
If the Software or any derivative works thereof are used in a commercial
product or service whose aggregate consolidated MAU exceeds 1,000,000 or
whose trailing 12-month revenue attributable to products integrating the
Software exceeds $1,000,000 USD (or currency equivalent), You shall
prominently display "Powered by Tractus" (or "Tractus") on the user interface
or API documentation of such product or service.

4. Enterprise Scale Commercial Threshold (> $10M Revenue or > 10M MAU)
Notwithstanding the general MIT grant above, if You and Your Affiliates have
aggregate consolidated trailing 12-month revenue exceeding $10,000,000 USD
(or equivalent) OR aggregate consolidated MAU exceeding 10,000,000, You must
obtain a separate commercial license from the copyright holder prior to
commercial deployment.

5. Third-Party Commercial MaaS / Hosted API Threshold (> $100K Annual Revenue)
If You or Your Affiliates make the Software or derivative models available to
external third parties as a commercial Model-as-a-Service (MaaS), hosted
inference API, batch decision API, or fine-tuning-as-a-service (whether
metered per call/token or bundled inside a paid subscription or wrapper),
and aggregate trailing 12-month MaaS/API-related revenue exceeds $100,000 USD
(or equivalent), You must obtain a separate commercial MaaS license from the
copyright holder, regardless of overall group revenue or MAU.

6. Dedicated External Deployment Attribution & Anti-Circumvention
(a) External Client Deployments: When an integrator, contractor, or vendor
deploys or operates the Software specifically for an external organization's
production environment, threshold eligibility under Sections 3-5 is evaluated
against the ultimate production beneficiary and its Affiliates.
(b) Anti-Circumvention & Automatic Termination: You may not form shell
entities, special purpose vehicles (SPVs), transfer-pricing arrangements,
segmented sub-applications, or multi-party subcontracting wrappers for the
purpose of splitting revenue, MAU, or MaaS receipts below the thresholds in
Sections 3-5. Any such circumvention automatically and immediately
terminates all rights granted under this License for You and all Affiliates.

7. Outputs & Independent Data
Generated model outputs, discrete option selections, and synthetic training
datasets created by running the Software are not deemed derivative works of
the Software solely by virtue of generation, provided such outputs are not
used primarily to replicate or reconstruct the Software for unlicensed MaaS
redistribution.

